    "body": "The shared language interface previously rejected a third question clause despite generic clause/query advancement in the existing runtime. Admit up to three clauses within the unchanged byte/word/read/step limits, and qualify the unchanged reader/updater/scheduler/writer with a separate Rust depth-transfer corpus. Add scoped second-update controls that preserve the first transition and incoming second state/source while disabling the new commitment or using a stale first payload.\n\n**PASS_THIRD_LANGUAGE_READ:** 1,280/1,280 answers and exact three-source paths; all 64 twenty-row intervention families. Both scoped controls lose all 1,280 successes. Full traces require two silent Reads, read counts1→2→3, both selected intermediates, continuous state and emission only at the third clause. Candidate bytes exactly equal parent62da0bfaddb37452a5ec7eb1aa220fbda7b33c79ef3dbcd4da1dcb11293e7a95. No fit, parameter edits or retry.\n\nValidation: release offline uor-r4-core build, one new and37retained focused tests; actual frozen-artifact generation/control report with13sealed files; all earlier controls preserved, including9,984dependent plus separate19,968scheduling and19,968credit rows; source/binary/reload preservation; formatting, claim wording and diff checks passed. All48prior sealed roots/1,221files and original dirty checkouts remain unchanged. Queue statuses are compatibility acknowledgements, not test evidence.\n\nComplete model/build/evaluation charge220,541/1,800,000ms. No allowance extension, paid compute or cleanup. This is bounded depth transfer with familiar vocabulary/grammar and explicit sequential references, not arbitrary discourse, general prose or metric advantage. ExactIdentity and FeedbackDisabled still pass fully. Normal15baec48 remains unpromoted; independent final holdout NOT_RUN.\n\nResult/evidence and current project documents record the scope and next diagnostic: completed answer versus an unresolved required continuation. The latter is a source-level predicted ambiguity, not a newly measured failure. No automatic extra depth ladder or broader answer writer is added.\n\nReferences #973\n",
